From: ThaRae <tharae@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:44:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] LibWeb: Keep an isolated world's thrown primitives to itself

An exception of an embedder's isolated world only goes to the
console -- but the check looked at the thrown value's realm, so a
listener of the world's that threw a primitive ("throw \"...\"")
had no realm to look at, and the value went on to the document's
global error handlers: the page could read what the world's scripts
threw, and that they threw. Objects were kept out, values weren't.

The global an exception is reported on is the throwing callback's
realm's global, so check that realm too: an isolated world reporting
on its own global goes to the console whatever it threw.
---
 Libraries/LibWeb/HTML/Scripting/ExceptionReporter.cpp | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Libraries/LibWeb/HTML/Scripting/ExceptionReporter.cpp b/Libraries/LibWeb/HTML/Scripting/ExceptionReporter.cpp
index 28e527562a843249f9b18ba4e47d6b0d599318e8..df31dd449c4a65cd5720e71cf60d73c04a8feba5 100644
--- a/Libraries/LibWeb/HTML/Scripting/ExceptionReporter.cpp
+++ b/Libraries/LibWeb/HTML/Scripting/ExceptionReporter.cpp
@@ -83,12 +83,15 @@ void report_an_exception(JS::Object& global, JS::Value exception, Optional<Error
     // AD-HOC: An exception of an embedder's isolated world, as from an event listener of its own, only goes to the
     //         console. The global's error handlers belong to the document's own scripts, and would get the world's
     //         objects.
-    if (exception.is_object() && IsolatedWorld::is_isolated_world_realm(exception.as_object().shape().realm())) {
-        report_exception_to_console(exception, exception.as_object().shape().realm(), ErrorInPromise::No);
+    auto& reporting_realm = relevant_realm(global);
+    if (
+        IsolatedWorld::is_isolated_world_realm(reporting_realm)
+        || (exception.is_object() && IsolatedWorld::is_isolated_world_realm(exception.as_object().shape().realm()))) {
+        report_exception_to_console(exception, reporting_realm, ErrorInPromise::No);
         return;
     }
 
-    auto& realm = relevant_realm(global);
+    auto& realm = reporting_realm;
     auto& vm = realm.vm();
 
     // NB: Whatever comes out of an aborted script is no error of its own.
